<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">Songs in History</h1><p class="ref-lede">419 songs that people have sung and handed down, in 101 languages, from a Sumerian hymn to the goddess of beer, copied about 1800 BCE, to songs of the last years of apartheid and of the Cold War. Each gives who made it, where and in what language, its story, what it says and the songs it led to.</p><p class="ref-lede sg-lede-words">The words of <b>286</b> are printed here, imported from free editions and never typed: in the original and, for the songs not in English, romanized and translated line by line. For <b>86</b> more, still in copyright or with no free edition yet, Genius shows the lyrics at the press of a button (and, for 22 not sung in English, its English translation), under its own licence. The other 47 have no words here yet (32 still in copyright, 14 in the public domain with no free edition found, 1 withheld, the page saying why). <b>380</b> have a performance to listen to.</p></header>
