<section class="sg-sec sg-fam"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Songs that led to songs</h2><p>Tunes travel: an anthem borrows a hymn&#8217;s melody, a farewell song becomes a graduation song on the other side of the world. These are the links between the songs in this library; every song&#8217;s page lists many more.</p><ul class="sg-chain"><li><a href="/songs/great-hymn-to-the-aten">Great Hymn to the Aten</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/psalm-104">Psalm 104</a><span class="sg-chain-h">possible influence, argued by Breasted, Weigall, Assmann, Redford and Koller and doubted by Lichtheim and others</span></li><li><a href="/songs/song-of-hannah">Song of Hannah</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/magnificat">Magnificat</a><span class="sg-chain-h">many Christian scholars believe Luke used it as the basis of the Magnificat</span></li><li><a href="/songs/hanacpachap-cussicuinin">Hanacpachap cussicuinin</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/magnificat">Magnificat</a><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/heil-dir-im-siegerkranz">Heil dir im Siegerkranz</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (anthem of Prussia, later of the German Emperor)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/my-country-tis-of-thee">My Country, 'Tis of Thee</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/gott-erhalte-franz-den-kaiser">Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser</a><span class="sg-chain-h">inspired by (a different tune, written after Haydn heard this anthem in London in 1794)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/ode-to-joy">Ode to Joy</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/rise-o-voices-of-rhodesia">Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/auld-lang-syne">Auld Lang Syne</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hotaru-no-hikari">Hotaru no Hikari</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune, Japanese words</span></li><li><a href="/songs/gott-erhalte-franz-den-kaiser">Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/deutschlandlied">Deutschlandlied</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hatikvah">Hatikvah</a><span class="sg-chain-h">named as inspired by it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/o-tannenbaum">O Tannenbaum</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-red-flag">The Red Flag</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/solidarity-forever">Solidarity Forever</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/john-browns-body">John Brown's Body</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a><span class="sg-chain-h">new words, same tune; written November 1861, published February 1862</span></li><li><a href="/songs/john-browns-body">John Brown's Body</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/solidarity-forever">Solidarity Forever</a><span class="sg-chain-h">new words, same tune; anthem of the Industrial Workers of the World</span></li><li><a href="/songs/warszawianka">Warszawianka (Whirlwinds of Danger)</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/a-las-barricadas">A las Barricadas</a><span class="sg-chain-h">Spanish version</span></li><li><a href="/songs/botany-bay">Botany Bay</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/waltzing-matilda">Waltzing Matilda</a><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><a href="/songs/polyushko-pole">Polyushko-pole</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/meadowlands">Meadowlands</a><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version</span></li><li><a href="/songs/polyushko-pole">Polyushko-pole</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/meadowlands">Meadowlands</a><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><a href="/songs/mbube">Mbube</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight</a><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as, Linda's closing notes made the new tune, with English words by George David Weiss</span></li><li><a href="/songs/mbube">Mbube</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight</a><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><a href="/songs/mbube">Mbube</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight</a><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><a href="/songs/without-the-communist-party-there-would-be-no-new-china">Without the Communist Party, There Would Be No New China</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-east-is-red">The East Is Red</a><span class="sg-chain-h">included in</span></li><li><a href="/songs/ode-to-the-motherland">Ode to the Motherland</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-east-is-red">The East Is Red</a><span class="sg-chain-h">closing number</span></li><li><a href="/songs/great-hymn-to-the-aten">Great Hymn to the Aten</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/psalm-104">Psalm 104</a><span class="sg-chain-h">parallel text; Egyptian influence argued by some scholars, rejected by others</span></li><li><a href="/songs/song-of-hannah">Song of Hannah</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/magnificat">Magnificat</a><span class="sg-chain-h">its most pronounced allusions</span></li><li><a href="/songs/wilhelmus">Wilhelmus</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-british-grenadiers">The British Grenadiers</a><span class="sg-chain-h">a possible ancestor of the tune (Henry Grattan Flood)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/heil-dir-im-siegerkranz">Heil dir im Siegerkranz</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/gott-erhalte-franz-den-kaiser">Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser</a><span class="sg-chain-h">model (Haydn and Saurau wanted an Austrian song to match it)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/my-country-tis-of-thee">My Country, 'Tis of Thee</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hey-slavs">Hey, Slavs</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/gott-erhalte-franz-den-kaiser">Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/deutschlandlied">Deutschlandlied</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><a href="/songs/psalm-137">Psalm 137</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/va-pensiero">Va, pensiero (Chorus of the Hebrew Slaves)</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the libretto was inspired by it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/la-marseillaise">La Marseillaise</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/canto-degli-italiani">Il Canto degli italiani</a><span class="sg-chain-h">source of inspiration for the text</span></li><li><a href="/songs/john-browns-body">John Brown's Body</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the soldiers' song whose tune Howe wrote new words for</span></li><li><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/national-anthem-of-ukraine">State Anthem of Ukraine</a><span class="sg-chain-h">influence on the words, as scholars think</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-three-ravens">The Three Ravens</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/when-johnny-comes-marching-home">When Johnny Comes Marching Home</a><span class="sg-chain-h">possible connection (Jonathan Lighter)</span></li><li><a href="/songs/la-marseillaise">La Marseillaise</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-internationale">The Internationale</a><span class="sg-chain-h">Pottier wrote the words to be sung to its tune</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hawaii-ponoi">Hawaiʻi Ponoʻī</a><span class="sg-chain-h">melody reminiscent of it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/heil-dir-im-siegerkranz">Heil dir im Siegerkranz</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hawaii-ponoi">Hawaiʻi Ponoʻī</a><span class="sg-chain-h">melody reminiscent of it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/kimigayo">Kimigayo</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the words may have been chosen for their likeness to it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/auld-lang-syne">Auld Lang Syne</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/hotaru-no-hikari">Hotaru no Hikari</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/sansoen-phra-barami">Sansoen Phra Barami</a><span class="sg-chain-h">Siam's royal honour music before this anthem</span></li><li><a href="/songs/marcha-real">Marcha Real</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/lupang-hinirang">Lupang Hinirang (Chosen Land)</a><span class="sg-chain-h">one of three pieces Felipe said he based the music on</span></li><li><a href="/songs/la-marseillaise">La Marseillaise</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/lupang-hinirang">Lupang Hinirang (Chosen Land)</a><span class="sg-chain-h">one of three pieces Felipe said he based the music on</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/land-of-hope-and-glory">Land of Hope and Glory</a><span class="sg-chain-h">first five notes similar</span></li><li><a href="/songs/john-browns-body">John Brown's Body</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/solidarity-forever">Solidarity Forever</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune</span></li><li><a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/solidarity-forever">Solidarity Forever</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune</span></li><li><a href="/songs/warszawianka">Warszawianka (Whirlwinds of Danger)</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/a-las-barricadas">A las Barricadas</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody; the Spanish words were based on a German translation of its Polish text</span></li><li><a href="/songs/la-marseillaise">La Marseillaise</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/thai-national-anthem">Thai National Anthem</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the model asked for by Luang Nithetkolakit</span></li><li><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/thai-national-anthem">Thai National Anthem</a><span class="sg-chain-h">melody vaguely similar</span></li><li><a href="/songs/auld-lang-syne">Auld Lang Syne</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/aegukga">Aegukga</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the tune the words were sung to before 1935</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-internationale">The Internationale</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/march-of-the-volunteers">March of the Volunteers</a><span class="sg-chain-h">opening motif inspired by it</span></li><li><a href="/songs/aegukga">Aegukga</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/aegukka">Aegukka (North Korea)</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the earlier anthem it replaced in North Korea</span></li><li><a href="/songs/mbube">Mbube</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight</a><span class="sg-chain-h">the original; Linda's final improvised notes became the new tune</span></li><li><a href="/songs/psalm-137">Psalm 137</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/jerusalem-of-gold">Jerusalem of Gold</a><span class="sg-chain-h">line drawn from</span></li><li><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/glory-to-hong-kong">Glory to Hong Kong</a><span class="sg-chain-h">model named by the composer</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-star-spangled-banner">The Star-Spangled Banner</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/glory-to-hong-kong">Glory to Hong Kong</a><span class="sg-chain-h">model named by the composer</span></li><li><a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a> <span class="sg-fam-arrow" aria-label="led to">&rarr;</span> <a href="/songs/glory-to-hong-kong">Glory to Hong Kong</a><span class="sg-chain-h">model named by the composer</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec sg-howto"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">How the songs are told</h2><p>The words of a song appear only where they are in the public domain: traditional and anonymous songs, and words whose authors died long ago or that were published before 1930. They are imported from the editions that hold them (Wikisource, Project Gutenberg, or the public-domain words quoted in Wikipedia&#8217;s articles), never typed from memory, and each names its edition. Where no older translation is free to use, the English and the romanization are the Institute&#8217;s own, made line by line from the original; notes say where a line can be read more than one way. Songs whose words are still in copyright have their story and their theme, told in our own words, but not their words.</p><p>Each performance was chosen by ear and by its source: the performers&#8217; own channels, choirs, ensembles and institutions, and old recordings. YouTube&#8217;s player loads only when you press play.</p></section>
